      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that they're different, but u cant really say they're equal in a modern context, right? it feels like retributive justice is basically just based on old-school ideas of vengeance, whereas restorative justice actually addresses the root causes of crime. wouldn't you say restorative is the more \"evolved\" moral choice for us today?",
